ring-and-initializing-rnr52tqd3","summary":"The map data type is built into Golang, so we often use it. It lets us store some value (like the value in the example above) and retrieve it by looking up a key. By contrast, a map lets us take one set of things and set up a one-to-one correspondence.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/72f9d414258f31e20783800b433bb96a?_a=AQADKdt","num_upvotes":4,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-05-14T05:35:28.000Z"},{"id":"9V7SA2gVS","title":"A Comprehensive Guide to Structured Logging in Golang","url":"https://golang.ch/a-comprehensive-guide-to-structured-logging-in-golang/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/a-comprehensive-guide-to-structured-logging-in-golang-9v7sa2gvs","summary":"A comprehensive Guide to Structured Logging in Golang Structured logging involves producing log records in a well-defined format. Such log records are composed of key-value pairs that capture relevant contextual information about the event being logged, such as the severity level, timestamp, source code location, user ID, or any other relevant metadata.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/ddc990cc8147a4369d82c6b65cebff56?_a=AQADKdt","num_upvotes":7,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-04-29T04:56:39.000Z"},{"id":"sYaWwt0ym","title":"Demystifying Golang Channels, Goroutines, and Optimal Concurrency","url":"https://golang.ch/demystifying-golang-channels-goroutines-and-optimal-concurrencyauto-draft/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/demystifying-golang-channels-goroutines-and-optimal-concurrency-syawwt0ym","summary":"Golang Channels, Goroutines, and Optimal Concurrency The Framework are examples of how Go executes goroutines and channels. The code used in the following examples is available here. The examples below are based on my 8 Core development environment.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/c34818d741832eaadbc097372af8a59c?_a=AQADKdt","num_upvotes":4,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-04-22T10:34:06.000Z"},{"id":"jiq5OaxZn","title":"Become a Golang Pro with 10 \u201cDefer\u201d Tricks","url":"https://golang.ch/become-a-golang-pro-with-10-defer-tricks/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/become-a-golang-pro-with-10-defer-tricks-jiq5oaxzn","summary":"The defer keyword can be used in several advanced ways to improve the efficiency and reliability of your Go code. This post will explore ten advanced tricks for using delay in Go. From canceling events and releasing resources to printing the time a function uses and recovering from panics, these techniques will help you take your Go skills to the next level.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1681015006/e35efe5b167896a9beecb858980cac84","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-04-09T04:31:29.000Z"},{"id":"wHI7y3p1G","title":"Golang hash table that is faster and uses less memory","url":"https://golang.ch/golang-hash-table-that-is-faster-and-uses-less-memory/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/golang-hash-table-that-is-faster-and-uses-less-memory-whi7y3p1g","summary":"Golang hash table that is faster and uses less memory than Golang\u2019s built-in map. We\u2019ll cover the motivation, design and implementation of this new package and give you some reasons to try it. This blog is part of our deep-dive series on the Go programming language.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1680235923/e6d0bafe41e140bc0161fa505f0eb816","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-03-31T04:10:32.000Z"},{"id":"u6D040JpB","title":"A Golang based open-source, self-hosted feature flag application","url":"https://golang.ch/a-golang-based-open-source-self-hosted-feature-flag-application/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/a-golang-based-open-source-self-hosted-feature-flag-application-u6d040jpb","summary":"Flipt is an open-source, self-hosted feature flag application that allows you to run experiments across services in your environment. It can be deployed within your existing infrastructure so that you don\u2019t have to worry about your information being sent to a third party or the latency required to communicate across the internet.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1679630868/69997bb405c0bcf3af0091ffe766c5fc","num_upvotes":15,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-03-24T04:05:17.000Z"},{"id":"Kyn2m9tAq","title":"The power of single-method interfaces in Go","url":"https://golang.ch/the-power-of-single-method-interfaces-in-go/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-power-of-single-method-interfaces-in-go-kyn2m9taq","summary":"Single-method interfaces (SMI) in Go are a more general and powerful technique than HOFs. SMIs have proven to be a very successful software modeling tool for Go programmers, and you find them all over Go code-bases. The tree search example using SMIs is almost identical to the previous version.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/cfcdab8c449341a7496fb5e636c28960","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-03-19T04:28:14.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["josramnmorenolara","shamundev","microsaasexamples","nextaitool","techgsmsoftwares"],"opposite_handles":["felixrieseberg","xai","hamelhusain","hwchase17","skirano"],"similar":[{"id":"9ba3f959-a9d7-4e28-9bc6-c69aa0b75021","handle":"josramnmorenolara","name":"Arduino y voltaje!","is_squad":true,"x":-8.3212,"y":8.1594,"cluster_id":2,"posts_collected":26,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--aE5NeW8g--/f_auto/v1772894676/squads/9ba3f959-a9d7-4e28-9bc6-c69aa0b75021?_a=BAMAMiiu0","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":1.144453,"median_upvotes":0.0,"author_present_share":1.0,"hype_score":0.0,"avg_read_time":1.884615,"tag_diversity":0.192308},"top_tags_preview":[["iot",26],["sensors",26],["embedded",5]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-8.3235,-8.4265],"